From 85221434cc5c08b5b949eca9688f95595c0c6033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:12:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PartialQuadratureFunction: stride between the components

The values of a partial quadrature function may now be stored component
by component: ViewSpecifications::data_component_stride gives the stride
between two components of a point (one by default, values stored point by
point).

- The call operator returns the values of a point as a strided span
  (mgis::StridedSpan), valid in all the layouts: the functions of
  mgis::function read it without copy.
- getIntegrationPointValues and data return contiguous values: they throw
  an exception if the components of a point are not contiguous (check
  inlined, exception thrown out of line).
- getComponentStride, hasContiguousComponents, isDense, and a constructor
  allocating the values in a given layout.
- Copies, assignments, updates from grid functions, L2 projections and
  post-processings read and write the values through their strides.
- The evaluations of an evaluator may request a layout
  (QPEvaluationOptions::layout): a result already stored densely in this
  layout is used as is, otherwise it is copied in this layout.
